cc @fee1-dead for wg-const-eval involvement and since we spoke a bit about this before, I'm not sure if it's just an oversight that CTFE doesn't handle evaluating the const item's desugared for `struct Foo;` and `enum MyEnum { Variant }`.

In current rustc when writing `let a = Foo;` referring to a desugared const item for a struct/enum variant this isn't faithfully represented in the MIR as it gets lowered to a `thir::ExprKind::Adt` instead of a usage of the const item. This means that MIR never contains uses of these const items so this codepath was never exercised.

As part of the work for `min_generic_const_args` outlined in [this design document](https://hackmd.io/@BoxyUwU/BJ6_bfmD0) we make some const generic arguments no longer go through an intermediate MIR body. This means that cases such as `Foo<{ MyStruct }>` are now directly represented by a usage of the const item causing us to ask ctfe to evaluate these const items when it was previously not necessary.

