## Optional extra features

### Expanding to expressions

A third rule could also be added, btw:

```rs
({ $($tt:tt)* }) => {{
    cfg_match! { $($tt)* }
}};
```

This would make it so `cfg_match!({ ... })` would be expanding in the context of a `{ ... }` block, so that the `=>`-rhs of the invocation body would then be able to expand to expressions _anywhere_ (rather than just in end-of-block position):

```rs
let os_suffix = cfg_match!({
    windows => {
        " XP"
    }
    _ => {
        ""
    }
});
